## Conjecture: Higher-Order Extensional Extraction Dominance

For random well-typed simply-typed λ-terms over base types and arrows of depth ≤ 3,
saturation with β, η, and a semantically sound finite axiom set yields an extracted
term whose size is at most the β-normal form size in at least 80% of cases, while
preserving denotation in all tested cases.

**Computational test:**
- Generate 500 random well-typed terms.
- Generate 5 random type-correct equations validated semantically on finite test domains.
- Run bounded saturation.
- Compare denotation of original vs. extracted, and size of extracted vs. β-normal form.

**Falsification criteria:**
- Any semantic mismatch between original and extracted term.
- Extraction size systematically worse than β-normal form in > 20% of cases.
-/


